Now my mother walks through the house in Mexico.
It is a big house.
It is warm and filled with sun.
My mother has the phone.
She walks to a door.
"Look, Maya," she says.
"Here is your room."
She opens the door.
I see my old room on the screen.
My bed is there.
And my desk is there.
It is good to see my room.
I smile.
